WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Slide a thin section of a
leaf under the microscope.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:08.410
Cells everywhere: walls,
nuclei, chloroplasts,

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.810
layer upon layer of them.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.540
You have a sharp pencil and a blank page.

5
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.660
Where do you even start?

6
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.920
So why does a good biology drawing leave
out most of what you can see down the

7
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.300
microscope?

8
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:25.650
In this mission, you'll compare a poor
drawing and a good one of the same plant

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.430
cells, and spot what makes the difference.

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.330
Then you'll find where xylem and
phloem sit in a leaf and in a stem.

11
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.960
Your mission: explain why a good
drawing leaves out most of what you see.
